:::tabs
## The idea

#### A field guide to making things

Start with a question. Collect what matters. Give it a form someone else can use.

:::callout {info}
**Keep the useful parts close.**

Notes, code, diagrams, and interactive explanations can live in one document.
:::

## The details

:::accordion
**Does it start with Markdown?**

Yes. Headings, paragraphs, links, lists, tables, and code blocks are your starting point.

**What do I share?**

Export an HTML file with its styles and interactions included. Open it in a browser, host it, or print it.
:::
:::

Try the tabs. This is Taildown, running on Taildown. {small muted}
:::
:::

---

:::grid {cols-3 gap-lg}
:::container {full}
### :icon[type]{primary large} Readable by design

`{large bold primary}` says what you mean. Start with sensible defaults and refine from there.
:::
:::container {full}
### :icon[panels-top-left]{secondary large} More than a page

Tabs, cards, accordions, diagrams, and a full icon library. Compose them as your document needs.
:::
:::container {full}
### :icon[file-check]{success large} A file you can keep

Save the editable `.td` source. Export a standalone page with its styling and behavior, ready to share.
:::
:::

